# rpi-mirror.list — the Raspberry Pi packages LordOS mirrors into its own APT repository (arm64 only):
# the bootloader EEPROM updater and exactly what its Depends need that Debian 13 does not have.
# docs/UPDATES.md, "Raspberry Pi firmware packages". Imported by `tools/release/apt-repo.sh build
# <target> --rpi …`, which accepts a file only if its SHA-256 is the one below AND the one in
# Raspberry Pi's signed index (InRelease, key tools/release/raspberrypi-archive-keyring.pgp,
# fingerprint CF8A 1AF5 02A2 AA2D 763B  AE7E 82B1 2992 7FA3 303E). A new upstream version is a new
# line here (the old one may stay: the pool only grows), reviewed like any other change.
#
# Architecture "source" pins a source package by the SHA-256 of its .dsc: the .dsc and the files it
# lists (checked against Raspberry Pi's signed Sources index) go to pool/rpi/source/, unindexed, so the
# source of every copyleft package we mirror (MPL-2.0 kms++) is offered next to its binaries, and so is
# the source of Raspberry Pi's FFmpeg, whose binaries are in the Pi 5 image.
#
# package            version                      arch   sha256 (of the .deb)                                             licence (debian/copyright)
